xt\">Dental Implants</span></h3>","skin":"WRichTextThemeSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-mf2k4zx6":{"hasAnimation":false,"crop":{"x":0,"y":0,"width":6000,"height":6000,"svgId":"cf545b123b6e4523b228d62bfa0dea9b.svg"},"alt":"Image by Andreea Rus","width":6000,"height":6000,"uri":"nsplsh_8b98f036db694d23a17d1ebd772be567~mv2.jpg","name":"Image by Andreea Rus","containerId":"comp-mf2k4zx6","hasBgScrollEffect":"","bgEffectName":"","displayMode":"fill","link":{},"encoding":"AVIF","allowWebpAvifTransforms":true,"responsiveImageProps":{"fallbackSrc":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/nsplsh_8b98f036db694d23a17d1ebd772be567~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_100,h_100,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Image%20by%20Andreea%20Rus.jpg","srcset":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/nsplsh_8b98f036db694d23a17d1ebd772be567~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_100,h_100,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Image%20by%20Andreea%20Rus.jpg 1x, https://static.wixstatic.com/media/nsplsh_8b98f036db694d23a17d1ebd772be567~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_200,h_200,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/Image%20by%20Andreea%20Rus.jpg 2x","css":{"container":{"position":"relative"},"img":{"width":100,"height":100,"objectFit":"cover"}}},"containerWidth":100,"containerHeight":100,"isInFirstFold":false,"onClickBehavior":"goToLink","fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WPhoto","language":"en","compId":"comp-mf2k4zx6","mainPageId":"a4aio","trackClicksAnalytics":false,"popupA11yExperimentEnabled":false,"translations":{"expandAriaLabel":"Expand image","zoomInButtonAriaLabel":"Zoom in"},"zoomedImageResponsiveOverride":{},"allowFullGIFTransformation":false},"comp-mf2kbufg":{"html":"<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px; line-height:1.8em; text-align:justify;\"><span class=\"color_15 wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Dental implants are artificial tooth roots, usually made of titanium, that are placed into the jawbone to support a replacement tooth or bridge. They look, feel, and function like natural teeth, making them the most reliable and long-lasting solution for missing teeth. With proper care, dental implants can restore your smile, improve chewing and speaking, and help maintain healthy jawbone structure.</span></span></p>","skin":"WRichTextThemeSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"}}}},"nicknameToCompIdMaps":{}}